with.input:
Assemble the final session result JSON from the outputs below. Return ONLY a valid JSON object — no markdown fences, no prose, no extra text.

Required output shape:
{
  "state_snapshot": {
    "current_week": <next week integer>,
    "start_date": "...",
    "end_date": "...",
    "starting_capital": <number>,
    "investment_mandate": "...",
    "checkin_weekday_1": "...",
    "checkin_weekday_2": "...",
    "ledger": { "cash": <number>, "total_value": <number>, "positions": [...] },
    "session_history": [ { "week": <int>, "minutes": "...", "final_decision": "...", "ledger_snapshot": { "cash": <number>, "total_value": <number> } } ],
    "this_week_outputs": {
      "analyst": "...",
      "research": "...",
      "risk": "...",
      "pm": "...",
      "cio": "...",
      "minutes": "..."
    },
    "approved_trades": [ { "ticker": "...", "action": "BUY|SELL|HOLD|REDUCE|INITIATE", "shares": <number>, "approx_cad_value": <number>, "rationale": "..." } ]
  }
}

Data to use:

NEXT WEEK NUMBER (current_week output): ${outputs.current_week}

STATE FIELDS:
- start_date: ${state.start_date}
- end_date: ${state.end_date}
- starting_capital: ${state.starting_capital}
- investment_mandate: ${state.investment_mandate}
- checkin_weekday_1: ${state.checkin_weekday_1}
- checkin_weekday_2: ${state.checkin_weekday_2}
- ledger: IGNORE state.ledger (it is stale). Use the 'ledger' object (with usd_cad and as_of, and positions with price_usd and price_cad) from the Minutes and Ledger crew output below.
- session_history: ${state.session_history}

THIS WEEK AGENT OUTPUTS:
- Analyst: ${outputs.analyst_data_intake.raw}
- Research: ${outputs.research_lead_update.raw}
- Risk: ${outputs.risk_officer_review.raw}
- PM Proposal: ${outputs.pm_proposal.raw}
- CIO Decision: ${outputs.cio_committee_debate.raw}
- Minutes and Ledger crew (emit_state_snapshot task): ${outputs.record_minutes_and_ledger.raw}

Build the JSON using the above. For approved_trades, parse the APPROVED TRADES TABLE from the CIO Decision output. For the minutes field in this_week_outputs, use the write_minutes task content from the Minutes and Ledger crew output. For session_history, use the existing state.session_history array — do not modify or re-summarise it. Output ONLY the JSON object.

Expected output: A single valid JSON object matching the state_snapshot shape exactly, with no surrounding markdown, prose, or extra text. All string fields populated from the provided inputs. approved_trades is an array parsed from the CIO APPROVED TRADES TABLE. If any input section is missing or contains NO DATA, set that field to null rather than inventing a value.

tasks.description:
Read the session recap carefully. Extract from the portfolio ledger section every open position currently held. For each position record: ticker symbol, number of shares held, cost basis per share, and the total cash balance. If the session recap states the portfolio is empty or week 1 with no prior trades, state that explicitly. Do NOT search the internet for this task \ read only from the session recap text. Output a clean structured table of all holdings plus the cash balance.

Session recap:
{session_recap}

with.input:
Project configuration:
- Start date: ${state.start_date}
- End date: ${state.end_date}
- Starting capital: $${state.starting_capital} CAD
- Investment mandate: ${state.investment_mandate}
- Check-in weekdays: ${state.checkin_weekday_1} and ${state.checkin_weekday_2}

Current week number: ${state.current_week} of 24

Portfolio ledger (authoritative source of truth for all current positions and cash):
${state.ledger}

Full session history (all prior weeks minutes and decisions):
${state.session_history}

Using the above, compile a structured SESSION RECAP that includes:
1. Week number and where we are in the 24-week programme
2. LEDGER SNAPSHOT section: copy every field from the portfolio ledger exactly, including: cash on hand, and for each position: ticker, shares held, cost basis per share, current price, unrealised P&L. State total portfolio value. If positions array is empty or null, explicitly state: No open positions. Cash on hand: [amount] CAD.
3. Last week final committee decision and any action items (or First session - no prior week if week 1)
4. Brief note on cumulative realised P&L to date

Format clearly with a labelled LEDGER SNAPSHOT section so the Analyst can read exact share counts, cost basis, and cash balance without any ambiguity.

Expected output: A structured session recap with a clearly labelled LEDGER SNAPSHOT section showing: cash on hand, every open position (ticker, exact share count, cost basis per share), total portfolio value, last weeks final decision, and cumulative P&L context. If no positions are held, state that explicitly. If any input data is missing, output: NO DATA: session context returned nothing. Estimated, remembered, or example values are never a substitute for real data.

tasks.description:
Read the APPROVED TRADES TABLE in the CIO Final Decision. Build a JSON array of trades [{"ticker":"XXX","action":"BUY|INITIATE|SELL|REDUCE|HOLD","shares":<number or 0 if unspecified>,"approx_cad_value":<number>}]. Then call the apply_trades_to_ledger tool ONCE with ledger_json set to the current ledger below (use '{}' if it is empty or null) and trades_json set to that array. Return the tool's JSON output EXACTLY as returned, with no changes, no recalculation and no extra text. Do not apply any trade yourself.

Current ledger: {ledger}
CIO Final Decision: {cio_decision}
